      "content": "You can counter this by reframing the idea of national obligation as interconnectedness. Argue that global instability, poverty, and disease eventually ripple back, directly impacting our own security and well-being. A strong nation does not quarantine itself; it participates in the global human ecosystem. Therefore, confronting crises abroad is not neglecting home, but actively fortifying our own future by upholding universal decency.",
      "source": "target",
